(`StepInterface.statement_of_steps`) splits every rough sample by hidden curvature, keeps a
curvature case carrying half the selected mass cofinally at every slack, and normalizes:

* low curvature (`LowStep.lowStep`, from x0398's `LowSample.low_sample_normalization`): one global
  power bin of the derivative size, test `R / v`, derivative-floor deletion charged to the
  original priors; depth `L - 4a`;
* high curvature (`HighStep.highStep`): the affine critical-center test `(B / ∂₃∂₃R) ∂₃R`;
  depth `L - 12a`.
-/

